
//Class: this will hold only and only concrete methods
//Abstract Class: can hold Concrete + Abstract Methods both
//Interface: this will hold only and only Abstract Methods


Base[addition/subtraction/multiplication/division] --extends-> A/B/C/D
Base(Abstract) [abstract addition(different)/subtraction/multiplication/division] --extends-> A/B/C/D
Base(Interface) [abstract addition(different)/subtraction(different)/multiplication(different)/division(different)] --implements-> A/B/C/D


Multiple Inheritance is not possible among classes in Java